{
  "id": "rs-beograd-subotica",
  "country": "rs",
  "category": "railway",
  "name": {
    "en": "Belgrade – Novi Sad – Subotica High-Speed Railway"
  },
  "description": {
    "en": "Reconstruction of the Belgrade–Subotica–Kelebija line for 200 km/h operation, the Serbian half of the Belgrade–Budapest corridor. Belgrade Centre–Novi Sad opened in March 2022 and the remainder to Subotica in October 2025. The Belgrade Centre–Stara Pazova leg runs on Serbian mainline 101 and the rest on mainline 105. The Chinese-financed legs were contracted in US dollars; the published estimate for Novi Sad–Subotica carries no price year, so it is omitted rather than assigned one. No cost is recorded for Stara Pazova–Novi Sad either: the only figure found for it, EUR 91.9 million, is implausibly low for a 40 km section carrying the Čortanovci tunnel and the Danube viaduct, and could not be corroborated. Mapped geometry for the northern lot stops at Subotica station rather than the Kelebija border."
  },
